  "id": "yohimbine",
  "term": "yohimbine",
  "definition": "Yohimbine is a biological agent described here as an alpha-2 adrenoceptor blocker, especially acting at presynaptic alpha-2A receptors. In endotoxemic mice, it increased cardiac norepinephrine release and was associated with reduced inflammatory signaling and less cardiac dysfunction.",
